<title>GREECE: Greece to cut next T-bill sharply, finmin sources.</title>
<headline>Greece to cut next T-bill sharply, finmin sources.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece will cut 40 basis points off the upcoming end-October 12-month T-bill rate, dropping it to 12.30 percent, finance ministry sources said.</p>
<p>This is in line with efforts to bring down the rate to 12 percent by year-end. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
